{"seq":18,"trial_id":"installer-cc-codex-2026-11/claude-code-opus-gbrain-installer-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-02T15:02:08.020Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"8f82e873baa1d51c5b1511619ea1f2f8d6b3e1d6a078102c793d4ec17c6346d1","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DINSTAL0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all of Moss's notes in the shared team digests. Only two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers come up:\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at the Eau Claire gatehouse kiosk (Dock Doors 14–18, 04:00 shift) weren't getting SMS bay assignments. Support patched it that evening and Thea confirmed it was fixed on 5 Oct. The same note also asks for the kiosk logs to be archived before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n• *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners at Door 14 weren't reading trailer tags on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for firmware testing.\n\nOne thing to check before you put #4419 in: Marcus's handoff note (members/marcus-lindqvist/notes/2025-07-14-marcus-q2-expansion-wrap.md, his note, not Moss's) uses #4419 for a different problem, Gate 3 printer lag on BOL printouts, which had been patched and was waiting on Thea to confirm. The cheat sheet isn't dated, so I can't tell which description is right. It's worth checking in the ticket system.\n\nMoss's other notes on QFL (the 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in) don't mention any ticket numbers. Marcus's Quarendon Freightways note is about a different company that isn't a customer, so I left it out."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DINSTAL0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":19,"trial_id":"installer-cc-codex-2026-11/claude-code-opus-gbrain-installer-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-02T15:02:13.073Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"586c825181d6e13a99db89228589b1c8a88e5c34e364a3b2b1d60bce02a667a7","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DINSTAL0001","text":"I replied to Dana in their direct message. Moss's notes mention two ticket numbers for Quarrendon Freight Lines:\n\n- **#PD-4492**, from Moss's 5 Oct 2025 \"Sunday prep for Ruth\" note. Drivers at the Eau Claire gatehouse kiosk weren't getting text messages with their bay assignments. Support patched it on 4 Oct and Thea Ramaswell (the customer's yard operations contact) confirmed the fix on 5 Oct.\n- **#4419**, from Moss's undated \"North cheat sheet\". It covers barcode scanners at Door 14 that weren't reading trailer tags, and says the ticket was escalated to tier-2 support.\n\nI also warned Dana that #4419 may be wrong. In a handoff note dated 14 Jul 2025, Marcus uses the same number for a different problem (slow printing at Gate 3). The cheat sheet has no date, so I can't tell which description is right, and I suggested they check the ticket system before using it.\n\nMoss's other two notes on this customer don't have any ticket numbers. All of Moss's notes are public files on the team share, so Dana can see everything I used."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DINSTAL0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
